From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NorkzYT <richard@pcscorp.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:21:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): hand the worker's own terminal its task
 identity (supervised terminal)

The dispatcher-owned worker's terminal tool used to be scrubbed like every other
spawn surface: HERMES_KANBAN_TASK/RUN_ID vanished and the delegate_task fence
marker was set, so a worker's own scripts could neither tell which card they
served nor record anything on it (`hermes kanban comment/create/link` all
refused). A worker read its own pid on the board as a "competing run" and
blocked.

Keep the fence on every surface, and add one narrow, verified path:

- agent/delegation_context: supervised_worker_terminal_env() re-attaches the
  worker's own TASK and RUN_ID (never the claim lock) plus
  HERMES_KANBAN_SUPERVISED_TERMINAL and the worker pid, only when the current
  process is the dispatcher-owned worker (not a delegate child, not cron);
  supervised_terminal_identity() verifies marker + ids + worker-pid ancestry.
- tools/environments/local + process_registry: only the terminal tool's
  foreground/background spawns use it; execute_code, MCP, LSP, codex, browser
  and cron spawns stay plain fenced descendants.
- base_session_env: HERMES_KANBAN_* and the fence never persist in the bash
  snapshot (they are decided per spawn), so a snapshot taken by the worker
  cannot hand its identity to a command issued inside a delegate child.
- hermes_cli/kanban + kanban_db(_connect): the supervised terminal may
  comment/attach/heartbeat/notify-subscribe its own card, create cards (tagged
  creator_task_id) and link cards it owns or created, after the board confirms
  the task is running under that worker pid and run. Lifecycle transitions
  (complete, block, request-review, unblock, claim, ...) and foreign cards stay
  denied; the DB-layer fence opens only inside supervised_terminal_mutation().

The grant is verified at the DB write boundary, not only by the CLI precheck:
supervised_terminal_mutation() records task, run (mandatory), worker pid and
a short expiry; every write_txn re-reads the task row and its run row inside
the transaction and denies when the task is not running under that pid and run,
the run row is missing or ended, or the grant expired. `link` requires both
endpoints in scope, with one verified exception the workflow needs: a card the
worker created may become another parent of a card its own card already gates
(the report card). A foreign card's graph is never changed otherwise. The grant
never covers board metadata; lifecycle stays denied for every descendant.
